2026-10-24 Charlotte Rösler  <charlotte_roesler@outlook.de>

	Made a load_data.cxx load_data.h and main.cxx file in src

	* load_data.h is the header for loading the data
	* load_data.cxx is the data loader using root
	* main.cxx is supposed to run the code, it does not work yet
	*The other files are suppposed to help the running process, will be removed because it does not run yet

2026-10-25 Charlotte Rösler  <charlotte_roesler@outlook.de>

	Made a run_weather.C and yearly_average.C file in src

	* run_weather.C is the working macro to run load_data.cxx
	* it stores the weather_data.root tree with all extracted columns from the data
	* main.cxx from last time is not inmproved, can be deleted, because run_weather took its job
	*Added yearly_average.C, which gives the yearly average over 200 years and plots a histogram stored as yearly_average_temperature.png
	*yearly_average.C not completely error free and not the final version yet.

2026-10-26 Herman Plank  <herman@plank.se>

	Made a yearly_extremes.C file in src/ and added folder results/ for plots.

	*Added yearly_extremes.C, which produces plots over yearly and monthly extreme temperatures, stored as .png's in a new results/ folder.
	*yearly_extremes.C is probably not the final version yet, will try to improve and figure out if I want to represent the data in other ways.


2026-10-25 Love Hagerberg <louffi.hagerberg@gmail.com>

	Made a "Temporary_Analysis" File which reads the data averages the temperature of each day and plots how many instances a day is the warmest or coldest.

	Started with just a code that went through and plotted, then I added the averaging, then I added the comparison within a year. Finally I changed it so it takes in days that have less than three measurements and measurements that have the "Y" marking.

2026-10-26 Love Hagerberg <louffi.hagerber@gmail.com>

	Read through what everybody else had made cause I had only pulled from main rather than from Dev.

	Made Extremedays.cxx and .h with Temporary_Analysis as a base. Extremedays integrates the load_data files but not run_weather.

2026-10-27 Love Hagerberg <louffi.hagerber@gmail.com>

	Worked on making the datasets interchangeable for our analyses. For this, dataset_registry.cxx and .h were created, they pull the csv files when the name of the city is given. Then I created run_analysis.C to pull from the data_registry and then execute the temperature_analysis function in extremedays.

	Also started fully updating the makefile to compile all of the different files so you can run it on command.

	Finally I changed the run_analysis from a macro to a .cxx and .h file.

	Spent the rest of the day fixing bugs in and related to run_analysis to make the build work. E.g. making sure extremedays.h can do strings.

2026-10-28 Love Hagerberg <louffi.hagerber@gmail.com>

	Successfully made the build work after changing the makefile so it properly builds the library files separately from the  
	.cxx files. Also started linking all the functions through main so that main becomes the command to run everything.

	Also redid the changes from yesterday since I had been writing in old copies of the files stored in a different directory.

	Updated main so that you can add the city name after the command rather than changing the file itself.

	Changed the run_analysis to Run_Love_Analysis so that others can make similiar files that call their specific functions.

2026-10-29 Love Hagerberg <louffi.hagerber@gmail.com>

